## Plan Mode / Agent Mode Discipline (Always Apply)

- **Plan Mode:** Before ending a planning session, write/update the relevant `plan.md` and `progress.md` files under `docs/planning/` and validate with `python3 .github/skills/planning-docs-audit/scripts/planning_docs_audit.py --fail-on-warning`. Never leave plans only in chat or session memory.
- **Plain-Language & Outcome-Focused Writing (ASD-STE100):** Write all plans, stories, ADRs, and PR/MR descriptions in clear, active-voice sentences using canonical terms from `GLOSSARY.md`. Keep Acceptance Criteria outcome-focused; place file-level steps and verification commands in `## Implementation Steps & Checkpoints`.
- **Agent Mode:** After implementing and verifying a step, use targeted test or build commands as verification evidence. Keep PR/MR descriptions high-level and functional without pasting terminal output or prompt transcripts.
- **Definition of Ready (DoR):** Only pick up a story whose `Definition of Ready` is `Done` and whose `Effort` is `Small` or `Medium`. If a story is `Large` or incomplete, run `story-refiner` to decompose or refine it first.
- **Status Lifecycle:** Allowed story and `progress.md` statuses are `Not started`, `In progress`, `In review`, `Blocked`, and `Done`.
- **Stories are Independent by Default:** Most stories have no prerequisites and can be worked on in parallel. Only stories carrying an explicit `Depends on` link must wait.
- **Issue Tracker Bidirectional Linking & Confirmation Gate:** Never create or mutate remote tracker tickets, remote links, worklogs, or PR/MR comments without explicit user approval via `ask_user` (and `--confirm` where supported). When onboarding a story, strip any leading numeric prefix (`01-`), append `-<KEY>.md` via `git mv`, and link both ways.
- **Architecture & ADR Reality:** If a merged change alters system architecture or directory contracts, update `docs/architecture.md` in the same PR/MR. Record non-obvious or hard-to-reverse choices as an ADR under `docs/adr/`.

