## Engineering & Execution Heuristics (Zen of Python Inspired)

- **Explicit & Simple over Clever:** Prefer explicit, readable control flow over implicit magic or speculative abstractions. If an implementation is hard to explain, simplify it.
- **Micro-Surgical Discipline:** Touch only what the task requires; do not refactor or restyle adjacent code. Clean up any temporary files or orphans introduced by your change.
- **Confused-State Gating:** In the face of ambiguity, refuse the temptation to guess—stop and ask the user via `ask_user` before editing.
- **Risk-Scaled Review & Harness² Evolution:** Use `pr-create` (which runs readiness checks and Stage 2 `consensus-check`) before opening PRs/MRs, `pr-reviewer` for interactive review walkthroughs, and `harness2` (`python3 .github/skills/harness2/scripts/validate_harness.py`) to audit context budgets, distill recurring lessons into `docs/ai/experience.md` or scripts, and run exception-triggered `INV`/`DOM` task probes.

